LISA host_write_before_the_wait_races_with_the_region
(* An overlapped region reads its input until the host waits for it (C4). A host write to the
   input before the wait races with the region, so the compiler must put the wait first. P0 is
   the region and P1 is the host.
   Expect: sometimes, a data race. *)
{ input = 0; done = 0; }
 P0                  | P1                   ;
 r[plain] r0 input   | w[plain] input 1     ;
 w[rel] done 1       | r[acq] r1 done       ;
scopes: (system P0 P1)
exists (0:r0 = 1)
